We Claim:

1.	A system for tracking phases of anesthesia delivery over a case for a patient, comprising:
one or more processors; and
memory storing instructions executable by the one or more processors to:
output (802), for display on a display device, a graphical user interface (GUI) including a first visual representation of a default or previously-determined phase of anesthesia delivery for the patient;
receive (602) a plurality of monitoring parameters of the patient over an observation window, at least a portion of the plurality of monitoring parameters obtained from an anesthesia delivery machine;
identify (606), by applying a set of rules to the plurality of monitoring parameters, whether an event signaling a change to a new phase of anesthesia delivery for the patient is detected, wherein the event is one of case start, maintenance start, emergence start, and case end;
based on the event being detected and determined to be a true event, update (617) the GUI to display a second visual representation of the new phase; and
based on the event not being detected, maintain (810) the first visual representation on the GUI.

2.	The system of claim 1, wherein executing the instructions to apply the set of rules to identify whether the event is detected comprises:
	applying (702) a first subset of rules to determine if case start is detected; 
applying (704, 706) a second subset of rules and a third subset of rules to determine if maintenance start is detected; 
applying (708, 710) a fourth subset of rules and a fifth subset of rules to determine if emergence start is detected; and
applying (712) a sixth subset of rules to determine if case end is detected.

3.	The system of claim 2, wherein: 
applying (702) the first subset of rules to determine if case start is detected comprises determining that case start is detected responsive to an end of a first standby event of the anesthesia delivery machine;
	applying (704, 706) the second subset of rules and the third subset of rules to determine if maintenance start is detected comprises determining that maintenance start is detected responsive to a first of: (a) and (b) being true or (c) being true, wherein (a) comprises a mechanical ventilation start event occurring, (b) comprises at least one valid value of end-tidal carbon dioxide (EtCO2), and (c) comprises a fresh gas flow pattern of: two initial fresh gas flow values being above a threshold, at least three out of the next five fresh gas flow values being below the threshold, and a third fresh gas flow value being below the threshold;
applying (708, 710) the fourth subset of rules and the fifth subset of rules to determine if emergence start is detected comprises determining that emergence start is detected responsive to a first of: (d) and (e) being true or (f) being true, wherein (d) comprises a mechanical ventilation end event occurring and observed for a threshold amount of time, (e) comprises no cardiac bypass mode, and (f) comprises two of an increase in O2 percentage, an increase in fresh gas flow, and an end of anesthetic agent delivery being true; and
applying (712) the sixth subset of rules to determine if case end is detected comprises determining that case end is detected responsive to a start of a second standby event of the anesthesia delivery machine.

4.	The system of claim 3, wherein the second subset of rules and the third subset of rules are applied in parallel, and wherein the fourth subset of rules and the fifth subset of rules are applied in parallel.

5.	The system of claim 3, wherein updating the GUI to display the second visual representation of the new phase based on the event being detected and determined to be a true event comprises:
if case start is detected (808), determining that the case start is a true event and updating (812) the GUI to display the second visual representation, the second visual representation indicating that the patient is currently in induction, regardless of the previously-determined phase of anesthesia delivery;
if maintenance start is detected (814), determining that the maintenance start is a true event and updating (816) the GUI to display the second visual representation, the second visual representation indicating that the patient is currently in maintenance, regardless of the previously-determined phase of anesthesia delivery;
if emergence start is detected during maintenance (818, 820), determining that the emergence start is a true event and updating (822) the GUI to display the second visual representation, the second visual representation indicating that the patient is currently in emergence;
if emergence start is detected during induction (818, 820), determining that the emergence start is not a true event, and maintaining (828) the first visual representation on the GUI;
if case end is detected (840), determining that the case end is a true event, and updating (842) the GUI to display the second visual representation, the second visual representation indicating that the patient is currently in case end, regardless of the previously-determined phase of anesthesia delivery; and
if none of case start, maintenance start, emergence start, and case end is detected, maintaining (810) the first visual representation on the GUI.

6.	The system of claim 3, wherein the event is case end, and responsive to case end being detected, marking the case as complete and applying (620) a seventh subset of rules to retrospectively update a timing and/or occurrence of one or more phases of anesthesia delivery for the case, wherein applying the seventh subset of rules to retrospectively update a timing and/or occurrence of one or more phases of anesthesia delivery for the case comprises:
	if more than one instance of a given type of event was detected during the case, selecting one instance of the given type of event as a valid event and updating the timing of a phase corresponding to the given type of event; and
	if no instance of a given type of event was detected during the case, adding the given type of event and updating the occurrence of the phase corresponding to the given type of event.

7.	The system of claim 6, wherein the given type of event is maintenance start, such that if more than one instance of maintenance start is detected during the case, one instance of maintenance start is selected as the valid event, where selecting the one instance of maintenance start comprises, if a duration of the case is greater than a threshold duration, selecting (906) a last instance of maintenance start that occurred during a first time period of the case. 

8.	The system of claim 7, wherein if no instance of maintenance start is detected during the case, adding maintenance start to the case comprises:
	if the duration of the case is within a threshold range, designating (910) a first predefined amount of time since case start as maintenance; and
if the duration of the case is greater than the threshold range, designating (912) a second predefined amount of time since case start as maintenance, the second predefined amount of time greater than the first predefined amount of time.

9.	The system of claim 8, wherein the given type of event is emergence start, such that if more than one instance of emergence start is detected during the case, one instance of emergence start is selected as the valid event, where selecting the one instance of emergence start comprises: 
if a duration of the case is greater than a threshold duration, selecting (916) a first instance of emergence start that occurred during a last time period of the case; and
if the duration of the case is greater than the threshold duration and no instances of emergence start were detected in the last time period of the case, selecting (918) the last instance of emergence start detected during the case. 

10.	The system of claim 9, wherein if no instance of emergence start is detected during the case, adding emergence start to the case comprises determining a time at which delivery of anesthetic agent to the patient ended and adding (924) emergence start at the determined time.

11.	A method, comprising:
outputting (802), for display on a display device, a graphical user interface (GUI) (1000) including a plurality of timelines (1010) of anesthesia delivery phases, each timeline depicting anesthesia delivery phase as a function of time for a respective patient of a plurality of patients;
for a first patient of the plurality of patients, receiving (602) a plurality of monitoring parameters of the first patient over a first observation window, at least a portion of the plurality of monitoring parameters obtained from an anesthesia delivery machine;
identifying (606), in real-time and without knowing a current or prior phase of anesthesia delivery for the first patient, that a first event signaling a change to a new phase of anesthesia delivery for the first patient is detected based on the plurality of monitoring parameters over the first observation window, wherein the first event is one of case start, maintenance start, emergence start, and case end;
based on the first event being detected, updating (617) the GUI to add the new phase to a first timeline of the plurality of timelines, the first timeline representing anesthesia delivery phases for the first patient; 
identifying that a second event for the first patient is detected based on the plurality of monitoring parameters of the first patient over a second observation window;
determining, based on the first event and the second event, that the first event or the second event is a false positive event, and in response, updating the GUI to adjust the first timeline to reflect the false positive event.

12.	The method of claim 11, wherein the first event is emergence start, the new phase is emergence, and the second event is maintenance start, wherein determining, based on the first event and the second event, that the first event or the second event is a false positive event comprises determining that the emergence start is the false positive event based on the maintenance start being detected after the emergence start was detected (830), and wherein updating the GUI to adjust the first timeline to reflect the false positive event comprises removing (834) emergence from the first timeline and extending a duration of maintenance on the first timeline.

13.	The method of claim 11, wherein the first event is maintenance start, the new phase is maintenance, and the second event is case start, wherein determining, based on the first event and the second event, that the first event or the second event is a false positive event comprises determining that the maintenance start is the false positive event based on the case start being detected after the maintenance start was detected (836), and wherein updating the GUI to adjust the first timeline to reflect the false positive event comprises removing (838) maintenance from the first timeline and plotting induction on the first timeline.

14. 	The method of claim 11, wherein identifying that the first event is detected comprises:
applying (702) a first subset of rules to determine if case start is detected responsive to an end of a first standby event of the anesthesia delivery machine;
applying (704, 706) a second subset of rules and a third subset of rules in parallel to determine if maintenance start is detected;
applying (708, 710) a fourth subset of rules and a fifth subset of rules in parallel to determine if emergence start is detected; and
applying (712) a sixth subset of rules to determine if case end is detected responsive to a start of a second standby event of the anesthesia delivery machine.

15. 	The method of claim 11, wherein the GUI comprises:
an operating room status panel (1002) indicating a total number of patients in each phase of anesthesia delivery; and 
wherein each timeline of the plurality of timelines (1010) is color-coded to indicate different phases of anesthesia delivery, the different phases comprising induction, maintenance, and emergence.

1)	A fiber extraction device for sisal leaves, comprising:

i)	a platform 101 configured to be positioned on a ground surface, wherein a chamber 102 is positioned over said platform 101 accessed by a user for placing multiple leaves of a sisal plant;
ii)	a touch interactive display panel 103 installed over said platform 101 to enable said user to provide input regarding the quantity of sisal fibers to be extracted from said leaves, wherein an inbuilt microcontroller linked to said display panel 103 processes said input commands and determines quantity of leaves required for extraction;
iii)	a pair of robotic arms 104 configured on said platform 101 that are actuated by said microcontroller to grip a pre-defined quantity of leaves from said chamber 102 and position said leaves between a pair of vertical blades 105 arranged in a tilted orientation on said platform 101;
iv)	an artificial intelligence-based imaging unit 106 installed on said platform 101 and integrated with a processor for capturing and processing images of said leaves, respectively, for determining thickness of said leaves, wherein based on said detected thickness, said microcontroller actuates a pair of sliding units 107 positioned in between said blades 105 and platform 101 to translate said blades 105 for adjusting the gaps between said blades 105;
v)	a pair of telescopically operated grippers 108 arranged on said platform 101, wherein upon actuation of said sliding unit 107, said microcontroller actuates said grippers 108 to work in coordination to grip said sisal leaves and repeatedly pass said leaves through said blades 105 to obtain said sisal fibre from said leaves; 
vi)	a robotic gripper 109 is configured on said platform 101 to grip and position said obtained fibres on a motorized roller 114 installed on said platform 101, wherein said roller 114 is actuated by said microcontroller to rotate in order to wind said fibres on said roller 114; and
vii)	an air blower 110 mounted on said platform 101 is actuated by said microcontroller for blowing hot air towards said fibres to facilitate proper drying of said fibers.

2)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a suction unit 111 is configured adjacent to said blades 105 to generate a vacuum pressure for withdrawing residues coming out from the leaves during the fibre obtaining operation and collecting said residue in a receptacle 112 paired with said suction unit 111.

3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a weight sensor is installed in said chamber 102 to monitor weight of said leaves stored in said chamber 102 and in case said monitored weight recedes a threshold value, said microcontroller actuates a speaker 113 installed over the platform 101 to produce a voice command to notify said user regarding refilling of said chamber 102.

4)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a battery is associated with said device for supplying power to electrical and electronically operated components associated with said device.

1)	A check valve testing and analysis device , comprising:
i)	a platform 101 developed to be positioned on a fixed surface and installed with plurality of supporting legs 102 for supporting said platform 101 at a height from ground surface, wherein a holding unit 103 is arranged on said platform 101 that is accessed by a user for engaging a check valve with said holding unit 103;
ii)	an artificial intelligence-based imaging unit 104 installed on said platform 101 and paired with a processor for capturing and processing multiple images of surroundings, respectively, to detect dimensions of said valve, based on which an inbuilt microcontroller associated with said device actuates plurality of motorized clippers 105 integrated within said holding unit 103 for securing said valve with said holding unit 103;
iii)	plurality of water tubes 106 connected said holding unit 103, said water tubes 106 are connected with a water chamber 107 installed on said platform 101, wherein said water chamber 107 is integrated with a heating unit that is actuated by said microcontroller for heating water stored inside said chamber 107 for generating steam that is transferred within said conduits to test said check valve;
iv)	an electronically controlled valve 108 integrated with each of said conduits dynamically regulated by said microcontroller to control flow of superheated steam, wherein a flow meter is connected to both inlet and outlet steam conduits, said steam flow meters are used to measure flow rate of steam during testing process, enabling accurate monitoring of steam usage;
v)	a sound sensor integrated with said flow meters to measure sound generated by check valve under varying steam flow rates and temperatures, providing additional diagnostic information on valve performance, wherein a touch-interactive display unit 109 attached to upper portion of said platform 101, providing real-time feedback on physical characteristics of valve for accurate performance analysis; and
vi)	a corrosion detection sensor provided with said platform 101 to detect presence of corrosion over said check valve, wherein upon successful detection said microcontroller activates a speaker 110 mounted on said platform 101 to produce audio alerts to notify said user regarding said detected corrosion.

2)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein said display unit 109 is also accessed by said user to select operating modes and monitor status of said check valve.

3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a temperature sensor is integrated within said chamber 107 for measuring temperature of chamber 107 and steam, said microcontroller automatically turns off said heating unit and notifies said user if temperature exceeds a threshold value for safety purposes.

4)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein an ultrasonic sensor is integrated with said platform 101 and synced with said imaging unit 104 for detecting dimensions of said check valve during testing, providing real-time measurements of valve's physical parameters.

5)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a battery is associated with said device for powering up electrical and electronically operated components associated with said device.

1)	An assistive device for relocation of oil tanks, comprising:

i)	a curved-shaped frame 101 positioned on a ground surface and installed with a pair of telescopically operated rods 102, wherein multiple wheels 103 are provided beneath said frame 101 for allowing a user to maneuver said platform over said surface as per preferences;
ii)	a microphone 104 provided with said frame 101 for receiving voice commands of a user for assisting  in relocating an oil tank present in proximity from one place to another, wherein  a microcontroller linked with said microphone 104 upon receiving said user’s commands activates an artificial intelligence-based imaging unit 105 installed on said frame 101 and paired with a processor for capturing and processing multiple images of surroundings, respectively, to detect presence and dimension of an oil tank present in proximity to said frame 101;
iii)	a pair of C-shaped extendable member 106 provided between said rods 102, attached with said rods 102 via a motorized ball-and-socket joint 107, wherein based on said detected dimensions of oil tank, said microcontroller actuates said member 106 to extend and retract in a repetitive manner, in view of clasping said oil tank within said member 106, followed by energization of plurality of electromagnets 108 provided on an outer surface of said member 106 for facilitating secure attachment of said oil tank with said member 106;
iv)	an angle sensor installed on said frame 101 that works in collaboration of said imaging unit 105 to detect angle of said member 106 with respect to said oil tank, wherein based on which said microcontroller regulates actuation of a L-shaped pole 110 integrated with a hinge mechanism and configured between said sliding unit and member 106 to enable angle of said member 106 to be adjusted, for adjusting position of said oil tank;
v)	a base supporting panel 111 attached to frame 101 via telescopic link 112, said link 112 is actuated by said microcontroller automatically when said imaging unit 105 detects presence of an oil tank in periphery, wherein said base supporting panel 111 is equipped with plurality of motorized pop-out balls 113 located along its inner periphery, configured to extend and retract, enabling said panel 111 to engage with said oil tank and assist in lifting, rotating, and stabilizing said oil tank for further operations; and 
vi)	an ultrasonic sensor mounted on said frame 101 and synced with said imaging unit 105 to detect unevenness on ground surface during movement of said frame 101 over said surface, wherein said microcontroller actuates a damping unit 114 integrated between aid frame 101 and wheels 103 to absorb sudden shock and ensure stability of said frame 101.

2)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein based on detected dimensions of said oil tank, said microcontroller actuates a pair of motorized sliding units 109 provided between said rods 102 and member 106 to translate said member 106 over said sliding unit, in view of positioning said member 106 at an optimum position.

3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein based on said detected height of object/ oil tank, said microcontroller extends/ retracts said rods 102 for positioning a pair of handles 115 attached with said rods 102 at an optimum height, allowing said user to maneuver said frame 101 for relocation of said oil tank.

4)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a UV-sanitization unit 116 is arranged on said handle 115 that activates after each use, automatically sanitizing said frame 101.

5)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a weight sensor is installed to panel 111 and when weight of said tank exceeds a predefined threshold, said microcontroller generates an alert notification through a speaker 117 embedded on said frame 101.

6)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a battery is associated with said device for powering up electrical and electronically operated components associated with said device.

1)	A machine mounted curbstone plastering device, comprising:

i)	a body 101 developed to be attached with a curbstone machine, via high grade fasteners with grooves to distribute load evenly across said machine, wherein a pair of motorized wheels 102 are arranged on ends of said body 101 for providing mobility to said body 101 on a ground surface;
ii)	a microcontroller linked with ECU (electronic control unit) of said machine, for detecting movement of said machine, based on which said microcontroller regulates actuation of said wheels 102 to rotate in sync with said machine ensuring said body 101 smoothly follows said machine, around edges of a curbstone;
iii)	an artificial intelligence-based imaging unit 103 installed on said body 101 and paired with a processor for capturing and processing multiple images in vicinity of said body 101, respectively to detect removal of plaster from specific portions of said curbstone, along with position of plaster mixture positioned in proximity to said machine;
iv)	a vacuum pump 104 mounted on said body 101 for extracting said plaster into a container 105 associated with said pump for collecting said plaster, wherein said container 105 is configured with a chamber 106 storing water, said chamber 106 equipped with an electronically controlled nozzle 107 to dispense suitable amounts of water into said container 105, followed by actuation of a motorized stirrer 108 arranged in said container 105 for mixing said plaster with water, to ensure an optimum consistency;
v)	an electronically controlled sprayer 109 installed on said body 101 via an robotic arm 110 for positioning said sprayer 109 in proximity to said specific portions, wherein a hollow flexible conduit is attached with said container 105 and sprayer 109 that is actuated by said microcontroller to spray said consistent mixture onto said curbstone’s portions; and
vi)	a frame 111 attached with said body 101 via an extendable link 112 for positioning said frame 111 onto said sprayed mixture, in view of scrapping said frame 111 over said mixture for evenly distributing said mixture onto said curbstone’s surface, for filling said specific portions, thus properly plastering said curbstone.

2)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a moisture sensor is embedded in said container 105 for detecting moisture levels of said mixture, to ensure optimum consistency of said mixture is achieved.

3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a pressure sensor integrated into said sprayer 109 to monitor and regulate pressure applied to said curbstone’s surface to prevent uneven application of cement.

4)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a battery is configured with said device for providing a continuous power supply to electronically powered components associated with said device.

1)	An adaptable dog protection device, comprising:

i)	a circular frame 101 developed to be positioned on neck portion of a dog while said dog is outside said dog’s premise, wherein said frame 101 is integrated with an ultrasonic sensor for determining dimensions of said dog’s neck;
ii)	a motorized roller 102 integrated in end of said frame 101 and coiled with a strap 103 connecting ends of said frame 101, that is actuated by an inbuilt microcontroller to rotate for loosening/tightening said strap 103 for adjusting dimensions of said frame 101 to get properly fit onto said dog’s neck, wherein a laser measurement sensor is integrated on said frame 101 for monitoring dimensions of said dog’s body along with distance of said dog’s mouth from said dog’s neck;
iii)	a pair of extendable bars 104 integrated on said frame 101 that are actuated by said microcontroller to extend towards said dog’s mouth, wherein a plurality of motorized hinges 105 is integrated in said bar that is actuated by said microcontroller to tilt portions of said bars 104 for positioning a covering unit 106 integrated at end of said bars 104 in proximity to said user’s mouth;
iv)	an artificial intelligence-based imaging unit 107 installed on said frame 101 and integrated with a processor for capturing and processing multiple images in vicinity of said frame 101, respectively to monitor activities of said dog including eating waste or biting someone, in accordance to which said microcontroller actuates plurality of expandable curved flaps 108 integrated in said covering unit 106 to get expanded/contracted in sync with said imaging unit 107 for acquiring a grasp over said dog’s mouth;
v)	plurality of inflatable pipes integrated in inner periphery of said flaps 108 that are inflated using an air compressor for applying a pressure on said dog’s mouth to remain closed in view of preventing said dog from eating waste or bite someone, wherein a strain sensor is integrated on said frame 101 and flaps 108 for monitoring strain experienced on said dog’s neck and mouth, in accordance to which said microcontroller directs actuation of said roller 102 and flaps 108 to prevent any discomfort to said dog; and
vi)	a sensing module integrated on said frame 101 for monitoring vital health parameters of said dog and in case said monitored parameters deviates from a threshold range, said microcontroller generates a wireless notification over a computing unit wirelessly connected with said microcontroller to alert said user regarding said dog’s health parameters, wherein said user is also capable of monitoring real time footage of said dog via said imaging unit 107 to estimate exact situation of said dog.

2)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein said sensing module includes a FBG (Fiber Bragg Grating) and PPG (Photo plethysmography) sensor.

3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein an inflatable layer is fabricated on said frame 101 that is inflated via said air compressor for providing a comforting experience to said dog while wearing said frame 101.

1)	A blind spot detection device for four-wheeler vehicle, comprising:

