ii)	an inbuilt microcontroller on receiving command, actuates an artificial intelligence based imaging unit 102 having a processer, installed on said body 101 to capture and process images of said side view mirror in order to determine dimension of lower edge of said mirror, wherein in accordance to which said microcontroller actuates a pair of motorized clamps 103 installed with said body 101, to open/close to acquire grip on lower edge of said mirror;

iii)	an ultrasonic sensor installed on said body 101 to detect distance between said lowed edge of said side view mirror and said body 101 and in accordance to which said microcontroller actuates a telescopically operated rod 104 installed between said body 101 and clamps 103, to extend/retract in order to position said body 101 in an optimal position with respect to said side view mirror;

iv)	a blind spot mirror 105 installed in said body 101 by means of a telescopically operated bar 106 that is actuated by said microcontroller to extend and protrudes said mirror 105 out of said body 101, for providing view of blind spots around said vehicle that is not seen through side view mirror, in order to increase visibility of obstacles, that is hard to spot while changing lanes, merging, or turning, wherein a motorized ball and socket joint 107 installed between said bar 106 and blind spot mirror 105, that is actuated by said microcontroller on receiving command via said infotainment unit, to adjust angle of said blind spot mirror 105 as per said user’s preference;

v)	a radar gun 108 installed on said body 101 to detect speed of a vehicle running behind said user’s vehicle, wherein in case said detected speed exceeds a threshold limit, said microcontroller actuates a speaker installed on said infotainment unit, to generate audible alert in order to notify said user to change lane; and 

vi)	a turn signal indicating sensor installed within said body 101 and synced with said imaging unit 102 to detect direction in which said vehicle is turning and based on said detected direction, said microcontroller activates a series of LED lights 109 attached to said cuboidal body 101, to blink yellow colored light to signal said vehicle’s intent to turn, thereby ensuring clear visibility of turn signals to other drivers, for safer driving experience.

2)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a holographic projection unit 110 installed on said body 101, that is actuated by said microcontroller to project a hologram in space, depicting an appropriate way to attach said device with said side view mirror, that is to be followed by said user in fixing said body 101 with said side view mirror.

3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a gyroscope sensor is installed on said body 101 to detect angle of said body 101 and in case detected to be exceeding a threshold level, said microcontroller actuates a telescopic link mounted on said body 101 to extend for positioning a suction unit 112 attached with said link in contact with vehicle’s door, followed by actuation of said suction unit 112 to create negative pressure for securely attaching said body 101 to said vehicle and preventing it from falling off said side view mirror.

4)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a battery is associated with said device for supplying power to electrical and electronically operated components associated with said device.

