ii)	an inbuilt microcontroller linked with said panel 103, processes said command and actuates an artificial intelligence based imaging unit 104 having a processer, installed on said platform 101, to capture and process images of vicinity of said platform 101, respectively to detect placement of a bundle of said pipe;
iii)	an inverted U-shaped frame 105 installed on said platform 101 and configured with a pair of robotic grippers 106, that are actuated by said microcontroller to grip said bundle and engage with a pair of holding units 108 installed on said platform 101, wherein an ultrasonic sensor installed on said frame 105 detects dimension of said bundle in accordance to which said microcontroller evaluates a length of said sheet required for wrapping said bundle of said pipes;
iv)	a motorized roller 109 wrapped with a sheet, installed on said platform 101, that is actuated by said microcontroller to rotate in a pre-defined direction, to unwrap said sheet in accordance to evaluated length and a RPM (Revolutions per minute) sensor which is equipped with said roller 109, counts number of revolution made by said roller 109 while unwrapping said sheet, and in accordance to which said microcontroller monitors length of said unwrapped sheet;
