2)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a pair of motorized sliders 107 arranged between said platform 101 and frame 105, that are actuated by said microcontroller to provide linear movement to said frame 105, enables said frame 105 to travel along length of said bundle of pipes, facilitating process of wrapping, evenly over an entire length of said bundle.

3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein plurality of load cells equipped in said holding unit 108, to detect weight of said bundle, that is displayed on said panel 103, to notify said user regarding weight of said bundle, for allowing said user to use appropriate resources for handling said bundle. 

4)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a battery is associated with said device for supplying power to electrical and electronically operated components associated with said device.

1)	An automated Ophthalmic eyelid stabilization device, comprising:

i)	a platform 101 positioned over a fixed surface, accessed by a user to rest said head portion over said platform 101, wherein a touch sensor integrated on said platform 101 is activated by an inbuilt microcontroller to detect accommodation of said user’s head portion over said platform 101;
ii)	an inflatable member 102 installed over said platform 101 and linked with a motorized air compressor 103, wherein upon accommodation of said user’s head portion, said microcontroller actuates said air compressor 103 to inflate said member for providing comfort to said user’s head portion;
iii)	an artificial intelligence-based imaging unit 104 installed on said platform 101 and integrated with a processor for capturing and processing images of said user’s eye, respectively, to determine positioning of said user’s eye, based on which said microcontroller actuates a sliding unit 105 installed on lateral ends of said platform 101 to translate an L-shape telescopic rod 106 mounted over each of said sliding units 105 in vicinity to said user’s eyes;
iv)	a C-shape link 107 configured on free end of each of said rods 106, wherein upon positioning of said rods 106 in vicinity to said user’s eye portion, said microcontroller actuates said rods 106 to extend and position said links in proximity to said user’s eyelids; and
